  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "\"As a user attempting to moderate a group instance I would like to be able to quickly identify players who's avatars are creating disruptive and/or offensive noises so that I can request that they stop and/or take moderation action against them.\"\n\nIn the last few weeks, I have seen a large uptick in avatars with either obnoxious or incredibly offensive sound clips on them. Many of these avatars are otherwise inconspicuous up until the point that the users starts playing the sounds.\n\nIn a group instance with 40+ people, the only way that I can find to identify such avatars is going through people one by one and hiding then re-showing the avatars to see if the sound clips stop.\n\nThere are a couple of methods available for identifying players who are currently talking, which is very useful for identifying people screaming/slur-baiting/playing offensive clips through the voice channel. The most wonderful of which is in the current instance tab on the quick menu where the little user icons light up when you can hear their voice and then right next to them are the available actions to take.\n\nA similar feature to indicate active avatar sounds would be greatly appreciated as it would massively simplify moderation and reduce the time it takes to deal with bad actors.",
